      "palaeogeo_unit_reported": "north Gondwana, including Arabia",
      "palaeo_unit_proposed": "Gondwana-North-Africa-Arabia",
      "age_as_reported": "middle Přídolí",
      "age_basis": "mixed",
      "age_basis_detail": "The joint occurrence of Margachitina elegans and Pseudoclathrochitina carmenchui identifies the elegans global chitinozoan biozone. Acritarch correlation with Libyan Biozone 3 supports a middle Přídolí assignment. Spores indicate the Spanish EC biozone, whose broader range is middle-late Přídolí to earliest Lochkovian. No direct independent graptolite or conodont control is available for precise placement of the chitinozoan concurrent-range zone within the Přídolí.",
      "age_circular": false,
      "stage_min_proposed": "Pridoli",
      "stage_max_proposed": "Pridoli",
      "setting_as_reported": "marginal marine",
      "setting_class": "marginal-marine",
      "n_samples": "3",
      "reworking_status": "none",
      "notes": "Section 5.3 reports more-or-less identical assemblages comprising 52 species across the three samples; the combined list contains 10 cryptospore and 42 trilete/monolete entries, including open nomenclature. The paper does not provide a complete sample-by-sample occurrence matrix, so the combined list is retained without assigning every taxon to every sample. Plates 1–5 identify illustrated specimens by sample depth. Land-derived miospores are common overall; taxon-specific abundances are not supplied. Chitinozoans and organic-walled microphytoplankton are substantial components of this integrated palynological study. Samples yielded abundant, well-preserved palynomorphs of low thermal maturity, T.A.I. ca. 2+. The authors extend Aneurospora isidori, Cymbosporites multiconus, Iberoespora glabella and Iberoespora guzmani into the Přídolí. Devonomonoletes sp. is retained as an explicitly reported monolete spore. The spelling Brochotriletres is retained from the manuscript.",
      "locator": "Sections 2–3, manuscript p. 3; section 4.1, pp. 6–7; sections 5.3 and 6.1, pp. 10–12; Plates 1–5 and their captions, pp. 25–27",
